# The `build-viewer` tool (caos SPEC, "Tools"): build the static replay-viewer
# wasm bundle — the one the observatory serves — inside caos.
#
# The docs are a HERE-STRING, so editing them re-keys this tool's arg tree and
# NOTHING it builds.
HELP=<<END
Build the static replay viewer: compile replay-viewer/ctf_replay.nim to wasm32
with the pinned emsdk, generate wire_constants.js, and assemble the bundle the
observatory serves (index.html, league.html, the worker, the sprite art). Then
check it — every file the bundle must contain and every script tag it must
carry — and return dist/ as the result.

The toolchain is the upstream emsdk image pinned by digest (caos/emsdk), with
Nim and the project's deps arriving as two cached jobs rather than image build
steps, so an unchanged bundle is a cache hit. Nothing is handed in from the
host.

Wasm32 is not a smaller version of the native build: `int` is 32 bits and the
address space ends at 2 GB, so this bundle can break in ways no native test can
see. `test-viewer` is what actually runs it.
@param [build-salt] Force a rebuild — any fresh value (e.g. $(date --iso=s)) re-keys the bundle build and nothing else.
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/imgtools --worker1:@=worker.sh --nim:@=DEEP-DEPS/nim --help=$HELP
